   "diff": 1,
   "stimulus": "equilibrium-representations-s1",
   "q": "What is the earliest time shown at which the system is at equilibrium?",
   "options": [
    "40 s",
    "20 s",
    "60 s",
    "0 s"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "why": {
    "correct": "Equilibrium is reached when the particle counts stop changing. The first two identical snapshots are at 40 s and 60 s.",
    "options": [
     "Right: the counts at 40 s and 60 s are both 4 W and 4 W₂, so the composition has stopped changing.",
     "The counts change between 20 s (6 W, 3 W₂) and 40 s (4 W, 4 W₂), so the system was still reacting at 20 s.",
     "The system is at equilibrium at 60 s, but its composition was already the same at 40 s.",
     "At 0 s there is no W₂, so the forward reaction is about to change the composition."
    ]
   }
  },
  {
